@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title Bounded interprocedural exception flow and handler dispatch

skinparam backgroundColor #FCFCFC
skinparam component {
  BorderColor #495057
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F1F3F5
  BorderColor #495057
}

component "reserved Throw nodes\ntyped value evidence" as THROW #DBE4FF
component "unique represented calls" as CALL #C3FAE8
component "call_graph_sccs\ncaller-to-callee condensation" as SCC #C3FAE8
component "ExceptionSummary\n<latex>E_f \subseteq \mathcal{T}</latex>" as SET #FFF3BF
component "callee-first singleton\nor bounded SCC Kleene rounds\n<latex>E_f^{k+1}=E_f^k \cup F_f(E^k)</latex>" as FIX #E5DBFF
component "nearest lexical Try layer\nsource-ordered Catch clauses" as LAYERS #D3F9D8
component "exact / inherited type match\nor untyped catch-all" as MATCH #E9ECEF
component "reached_catches\naccepted type sets" as REACHED #D3F9D8
component "root SCC escaping type\nUncaughtException + witness" as UNCAUGHT #FFE3E3
component "unreached handler\nDeadCatch" as DEAD #FFE3E3
component "caps and issues\nqualified report" as QUAL #FCC2D7

THROW --> SET : direct type origins
CALL --> SCC
SCC --> FIX : stable component order
SET --> FIX
CALL --> FIX : join callee summaries
FIX --> SET : monotone finite union
SET --> LAYERS : direct + propagated origins
LAYERS --> MATCH
MATCH --> REACHED : first accepting catch
MATCH --> SET : no handler; type escapes
SET --> UNCAUGHT : source call component
LAYERS --> DEAD : no reached entry
FIX --> QUAL : function / fact / work / SCC caps
THROW --> QUAL : unknown nominal type
CALL --> QUAL : ambiguous target
LAYERS --> QUAL : missing typed Catch edge
UNCAUGHT --> QUAL : missing origin witness

note bottom of FIX
  Mutual recursion is a finite SCC fixed point.
  No call path is expanded on the native stack.
end note

note bottom of MATCH
  Inheritance closure uses an ordered heap worklist
  and terminates even when represented type edges cycle.
end note

note bottom of UNCAUGHT
  The canonical witness is the shortest stable sequence
  of entry, call, callee, and direct-throw node identifiers.
end note

legend bottom
|= Colour |= Meaning |
|<#DBE4FF>| typed throw evidence |
|<#C3FAE8>| represented call topology |
|<#FFF3BF>| finite exception-type lattice |
|<#E5DBFF>| bounded recursive summary fixed point |
|<#D3F9D8>| lexical handler flow |
|<#E9ECEF>| nominal type matching |
|<#FFE3E3>| advisory finding |
|<#FCC2D7>| incomplete-result evidence |
endlegend
@enduml
